      "author": {
        "id": 1165921
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-05T17:47:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is fine, but I do wonder why we need 64-bit timeouts\nIf this is microseconds then 4 billion of them is over an hour",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 126,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 126,
        "endChar": 14
      },
      "revId": "048bb28cb5b317a56fabc41616a5f3d982241598",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "02b9dad8_7884dc1f",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/src/tasks.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 126,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-05T18:07:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well that is the return type of k_uptime_ticks, so we would lose precision otherwise.\n\n(I have also code timing issues thinking we would never have waits over an hour before, and using int64 just prevents most of them)",
      "parentUuid": "5f125707_e6395f31",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 126,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 126,
        "endChar": 14
      },
